# Text is stored and checked out with LF line endings, whatever core.autocrlf says on the machine.
#
# Without this the tree's cleanliness depended on local configuration: Git for Windows sets
# core.autocrlf=true in its system config, under which the working tree reads as clean, while any git
# that does not read that config saw 163 files as modified that differed only in line endings. A
# clean tree could not be verified, and a `git add -A` from the wrong shell was a junk commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files already tracked. Never converted.
*.png -text
